(EXP-05: hexadecimal literals with the `0x` prefix.
 Also covers: EXP-06 binary literals with the `0b` prefix, EXP-07 character
 literals in single quotes, EXP-14 `0xFF` equals 255, EXP-15 `0b1010` equals
 10, EXP-16 `'A'` equals 65.
 The last two lines put hex and character literals in operand position rather
 than initializer position, since that is the position a leaf would emit.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-05.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   255
   3735928559
   180
   15
   10
   65
   33
   0
   66
)
